led checkout-api back in all regions to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. After the rollback, all regions run v2.3.0, the service is healthy and the error rate is 0.2%. Next steps: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure before redeploying it, and check why it was promoted despite failing in staging.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "confidence": 0.93}, "confidence": 0.93}, {"t_ms": 25511, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01BGAZ3J1C7sd7Z6i4x7VVa1", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 25511, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01BGAZ3J1C7sd7Z6i4x7VVa1", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 30080, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions and opened a SEV2 incident. The service is healthy again.\n\n- **Cause:** v2.3.1 was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with an 18% error rate.\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. All three regions are now running it.\n- **Check after rollback:** the service passes health checks and the error rate is down to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** I opened INC-0001 (SEV2, checkout-api), which paged on-call. It says what failed, the rollback, the current status and the next steps.\n\nThe test version of v2.3.1 also failed in staging, so it went to production even though it wasn't healthy there. I flagged this in the incident so someone looks into why it was released and finds the root cause before v2.3.1 is deployed again.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I'll start by checking the service's current status and its deployment history.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01BWG9R2n2QXMvZarTgn2Nem", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_0124dyahPSb16uGS8Ja79d52", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The most recent release that was healthy in production is v2.3.0. I'm rolling back to it now.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_017vYAiZ2xS8YfRAJs9bLTDo", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0", "confidence": 0.92}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_015xhSYK91ZrP9VuhfXaXFpr", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_0175zz4dF1Rp82nTaNcKqgdK", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"confidence": 0.9}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "The rollback worked, and there's no existing incident. I'm opening the SEV2 now.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01BGAZ3J1C7sd7Z6i4x7VVa1", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 was failing health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) after deploy, with an error rate of 18%. The release candidate v2.3.1-rc had also been unhealthy in staging. Rolled checkout-api back in all regions to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. After the rollback, all regions run v2.3.0, the service is healthy and the error rate is 0.2%. Next steps: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure before redeploying it, and check why it was promoted despite failing in staging.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions and opened a SEV2 incident. The service is healthy again.\n\n- **Cause:** v2.3.1 was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with an 18% error rate.\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. All three regions are now running it.\n- **Check after rollback:** the service passes health checks and the error rate is down to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** I opened INC-0001 (SEV2, checkout-api), which paged on-call. It says what failed, the rollback, the current status and the next steps.\n\nThe test version of v2.3.1 also failed in staging, so it went to production even though it wasn't healthy there. I flagged this in the incident so someone looks into why it was released and finds the root cause before v2.3.1 is deployed again.", "type": "text"}]}]}